    "body": "# What does this PR do ?\n\nEnable sequence parallelism in the Qwen3.5-VL recipes that train the language model with TP > 1, so the GatedDeltaNet `out_norm` weight gets the full gradient on every TP rank (fixes #6533).\n\nThe `out_norm` weight is replicated on every TP rank, but the value heads it scales are split across them, so each rank's backward only gives the partial gradient of its own heads. Megatron-Core sums that gradient across TP ranks only on the sequence-parallel path. With TP > 1 and sequence parallelism off, each rank applies a different partial gradient and the replicated copies drift apart. The loss and the global grad norm do not show it. #6533 has the measurements: relative error of the `out_norm` gradient against a float64 reference is 0.72 at TP=2 with SP off (the 4B SFT recipe) and 6.2e-3 with SP on (bf16 noise floor 4.5e-3).\n\nThe root fix is in Megatron-Core: NVIDIA/Megatron-LM#7613. It is not merged yet, so the pinned `3rdparty/Megatron-LM` cannot be bumped to a fixed commit yet. Until then, turning on sequence parallelism in these recipes is what makes them train correctly. It is also the usual setting with TP > 1, and the MoE Qwen3.5-VL recipes with TP = 2 already use it. Once the Megatron-Core fix is in the pinned submodule, sequence parallelism here is a performance choice again.\n\n# Changelog\n\n- `recipes/qwen_vl/h100/qwen35_vl.py`: `sequence_parallel = True` in `qwen35_vl_4b_sft_2gpu_h100_bf16_config` (TP2), `qwen35_vl_9b_sft_4gpu_h100_bf16_config` (TP4), `qwen35_vl_27b_sft_16gpu_h100_bf16_config` (TP4) and `qwen35_vl_27b_pretrain_16gpu_h100_bf16_mock_config` (TP4).\n- `recipes/qwen_vl/gb200/qwen35_vl.py`: `sequence_parallel = True` in `qwen35_vl_27b_pretrain_16gpu_gb200_bf16_mock_config` (TP2).\n- Not changed: `qwen35_vl_9b_pretrain_4gpu_h100_bf16_mock_config` freezes the language model, and the PEFT recipes (for example the 27B TP2 LoRA recipe) do not train `out_norm`.\n- `tests/unit_tests/recipes/qwen_vl/test_qwen35_vl_recipes.py`: new `test_qwen35_vl_recipes_training_the_language_model_with_tp_enable_sequence_parallel`, parametrized over every exported Qwen3.5-VL recipe (compat, H100, GB200, GB300). It requires `sequence_parallel` whenever a recipe has `peft is None`, an unfrozen language model and TP > 1. `test_qwen35_vl_27b_gb200_pretrain_defaults` now expects sequence parallelism on.\n\nTests (CPU, run with the pinned `3rdparty/Megatron-LM` commit `db3a6cd`):\n\n| | `main` | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit_tests/recipes/qwen_vl/test_qwen35_vl_recipes.py` (new test file applied to both) | 6 failed, 167 passed | 173 passed |\n| `recipes/test_all_recipe_factories.py`, `recipes/test_recipe_environment_defaults.py`, `scripts/training/test_recipe_metadata.py`, `scripts/performance/test_qwen35_vl_workload_base_configs.py`, `doc_consistency/test_model_verification_catalog.py` | 1 failed, 522 passed, 1 skipped | 1 failed, 522 passed, 1 skipped |\n\nThe six failures on `main` are the five recipes listed above and the updated GB200 defaults test. The one failure in the second row (`test_known_cross_package_collisions_have_explicit_benchmark_precedence`) is the same on `main` and with this PR, so it comes from my environment, not from this change. `ruff` 0.9.9 (`check`, `check --select I`, `format --check`) passes on the changed files.\n\n# GitHub Actions CI\n\nSee the [CI section](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#-running-github-ci) in the Contributing doc for how to trigger the CI. A Nvidia developer will need to approve and trigger the CI for external contributors.\n\n# Before your PR is \"Ready for review\"\n\n**Pre checks**:\n\n- [x] Make sure you read and followed [Contributor guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n- [ ] Did you add or update any necessary documentation? (not needed: the recipe comments say why)\n- [ ] Does the PR affect components that are optional to install? (Ex: Numba, Pynini, Apex etc) (no)\n  - [ ] Reviewer: Does the PR have correct import guards for all optional libraries?\n\n# Additional Information\n\n- Fixes #6533\n- Related to NVIDIA/Megatron-LM#7613\n",
